// Rules Mojo owns, reported by Mojo, at a Mojo column.
//
// Linearity is not checked twice. `Lin` is neither `Copyable` nor
// `Deinitable`, so using a qubit twice and dropping one are both ordinary
// Mojo ownership errors; qcc never sees these programs.
//
// REQUIRES: mojo-kernels
// RUN: not %kgen --elaborate -O1 --emit-quantum-kernels=%t %mojo_kernels/errors/drop.mojo 2>&1 \
// RUN:     | FileCheck --check-prefix=DROP %s
// RUN: not %kgen --elaborate -O1 --emit-quantum-kernels=%t %mojo_kernels/errors/double.mojo 2>&1 \
// RUN:     | FileCheck --check-prefix=DOUBLE %s
// RUN: not %kgen --elaborate -O1 --emit-quantum-kernels=%t %mojo_kernels/errors/early_return.mojo 2>&1 \
// RUN:     | FileCheck --check-prefix=RETURN %s

// A dropped qubit gets the library's own `@explicit_destroy` message.
// DROP: drop.mojo:13:29: error: 'dropped' abandoned without being explicitly destroyed: quantum values must be consumed: 'measure()', 'discard()', or pass it on

// A second use reads a binding the first use ended.
// DOUBLE: double.mojo:16:27: error: use of uninitialized value 'a'
// DOUBLE: double.mojo:12:9: note: 'a' declared here

// An early exit from a linearization body is a parse error, not something
// that reaches qcc: a `__mlir_region` body is not a function, so there is
// nothing for `return` to return from.
// RETURN: early_return.mojo:16:13: error: 'return' must be inside a function
